  "reflectionText": "Paul wrote: if I speak with the tongues of men and of angels and have not love, I am a clanging cymbal. Love bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, endures all things. Now faith, hope, and love remain; the greatest of these is love. How do you measure a life against the one thing that bears, believes, hopes, and endures, all at the same time?"
